# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# WHICH KEYS YOU NEED DEPENDS ON YOUR ROSTER.
# Every `model:` in adws/adw_sssf_config/sssf.config.yaml is written as
# provider/model-id, using the names `omp models` prints. The provider half
# decides which credential must be present.
#
# The starter roster names two providers:
#   openai-codex/gpt-5.6-terra      Codex OAuth — `omp` signs in, no key here
#   openrouter/moonshotai/kimi-k3   openrouter  -> OPENROUTER_API_KEY
#
# Point every agent at one provider and you only need that one credential.
# Setting `defaults.model` and deleting the per-agent `model:` overrides is the
# fastest way to run the whole roster on a single provider.
#
# Nothing validates the credential for you. `agents.validate()` checks that a
# model is written as provider/id and that `omp models` lists it — not that the
# provider is reachable or authenticated. A missing credential shows up when
# that agent runs, not at startup.
#
# A model that IS listed can still be substituted: omp 17.3.1 answers a request
# for openai-codex/gpt-5.6-luna by running openai-codex/gpt-5.6-terra. SSSF
# refuses that rather than recording a model that never ran, so a roster naming
# a substituted model fails at run time with a ModelBindingError.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Optional overrides
# OMP_PATH=omp                     # omp binary if not on PATH (PI_PATH also read)
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
